    "intro": "Starting a building firm? This **construction company name generator** suggests names for builders, contractors and renovation firms: catchy, classic family names, strong one-word names, modern and luxury, plus names from your town or your first name.",
    "sections": [],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do I check a construction company name is free?",
        "answer": "Press <strong>Check</strong> next to any name to see if it's free as a company, a domain and a social media handle. Then make sure: in the UK, search Companies House and the UK IPO trade mark register; in the US, search your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search. A quick map search for the name in your area helps too."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are some construction company names with meaning?",
        "answer": "Many of the best come from the trade itself. A <em>keystone</em> is the central stone that locks an arch together, a <em>cornerstone</em> is the first stone laid, a <em>plumb line</em> shows a wall is truly upright and a <em>lintel</em> carries the wall over a door. They suggest strength and careful work."
      }
    ]
